    "b-40-subagents-spawning-is-a-tool-decla-5": {
      "id": "b-40-subagents-spawning-is-a-tool-decla-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Spawning is a tool declaration, not an agent flag (D77)"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-subagents-decision-the-only-w-6": {
      "id": "b-40-subagents-decision-the-only-w-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " The only way an agent gains spawn capability is a spawner tool declared in its tools sidecar via "
        },
        {
          "insert": "defineSpawnerTool({ name, parameters, spawns, execute })",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "spawns",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " an explicit allowlist of agent names ("
        },
        {
          "insert": "[\"*\"]",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the loud general opt-in). The declaration compiles into an ordinary Pi-registerable tool; at session build time "
        },
        {
          "insert": "bindSpawnerTools",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " replaces the placeholder execute with one holding the scoped "
        },
        {
          "insert": "dispatch",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " handle. The agent-level "
        },
        {
          "insert": "canSpawnSubagent",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " manifest boolean is retired, and the generic Pi subagent tools are disallowed for every kernel agent."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-subagents-why-an-agent-level-7": {
      "id": "b-40-subagents-why-an-agent-level-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " An agent-level flag grants a capability without naming its targets, so nothing can validate the fan-out at boot and a typo becomes a silently errored record at runtime. A per-tool allowlist is boot-validated against the catalog and puts the grant on the action surface where the tool author already is."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-subagents-applies-to-package-8": {
      "id": "b-40-subagents-applies-to-package-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Applies to.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "packages/kernel/src/subagents/spawner-binding.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", spawner harvest in the registry, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "spawn-pipeline/pi-session-factory/tool-scoping.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " (which adds the generic Pi subagent tools, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "SUBAGENT_TOOL_NAMES",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", to every session's disallow list), and every future spawner tool: new spawn capabilities must be declared this way, never as manifest flags."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-subagents-agentmanager-takes-a-9": {
      "id": "b-40-subagents-agentmanager-takes-a-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 3
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "AgentManager",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " takes a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "spawnAgent",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " adapter"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-subagents-decision-the-manage-10": {
      "id": "b-40-subagents-decision-the-manage-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Decision.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " The manager does not import the spawn pipeline. Its "
        },
        {
          "insert": "AgentManagerDeps",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " require a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "spawnAgent",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " function and accept an optional "
        },
        {
          "insert": "traceWriter",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "subagentLinkCustomType",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". With a trace writer, the manager emits "
        },
        {
          "insert": "run_steered",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " itself for each accepted steering message, deferring the event until the run's trace identity is known. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "createKernel",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " passes its own trace writer when a db is configured."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-subagents-why-subagent-orches-11": {
      "id": "b-40-subagents-why-subagent-orches-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Why.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " Subagent orchestration (records, queueing, stop/cleanup, steering) stays independent of the concrete runtime host and testable without one. The rejected alternative (the manager calling the pipeline directly) makes orchestration and spawning one unswappable unit."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
